# partyplay.com.au cache rules (Cloudflare Pages).
#
# THIS FILE WAS NOT IN FORCE FOR .js UNTIL 12 Sep 2026, and nothing in it was wrong.
# The ZONE had Browser Cache TTL set to 4 hours, which overrides Cache-Control from here
# for everything that is not HTML. So /lib/pp-config.js came back "max-age=14400" while
# this file said no-cache, and the security headers below arrived correctly the whole
# time, which is what made it look fine. venueplay.com.au was already set to "Respect
# Existing Headers"; partyplay.com.au now matches it.
#
# It mattered because pp-config.js carries the Supabase key. A config fix could sit
# unreachable in a guest's phone for four hours, and a guest's phone at a party is the
# product.
#
# Copied from venueplay.com.au, where two wrong assumptions were each paid for once.
# Do not "tidy" this without reading the notes.
#
# no-cache (revalidate), NOT no-store (never cache). A no-store would force every asset
# to download again on every page view, on a phone, at a party, on someone's home wifi.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  # SAMEORIGIN, not DENY: the party screen embeds the game pages in an iframe from this
  # same site, and DENY would leave the host staring at a black television.
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Two things proved against the live VenuePlay site, which apply identically here:
#
# 1. Cloudflare Pages MERGES every rule that matches. It does not pick the most specific
#    one. A later rule can only ADD to /*, never override it.
# 2. Because of that, an "immutable" rule on /logos/* cannot work while /* sets
#    Cache-Control: per RFC 9111 a no-cache anywhere in the field forces revalidation.
#
# That is a deliberate trade. Dropping Cache-Control from /* would let a logo rule win,
# but /* is the only pattern reaching the extensionless routes Pages serves (/play, /tv,
# /host). A stale cached game page is far worse than a logo that returns a 304.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# The admin screen. Not linked from anywhere, but "not linked" is not a control.
# THE LOGOS ARE THE ONE THING WORTH CACHING HARD, and this rule has to exist BEFORE the
# zone's Browser Cache TTL is set to respect these headers, or every logo starts
# revalidating on every page view. At a party that is a phone on someone's home wifi, or
# on data, fetching the same mark over and over. They are content-addressed by name and
# change about once a year, so a year is honest. Same rule and same reason as venueplay.
/logos/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/admin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
